  The article gives a total subsidy of up to 50% but does not say the subsidy applies to every item; the draft's 'அரசு மானியம்' framing is fine, but the reel_script says 'Tamil Nadu tender greens' programme discount' as ரூ.1,200 தொகுப்பு ரூ.600 — article says ரூ.600 மானியத்தில் வழங்கப்படுகிறது, which means subsidy is ரூ.600 (price would be ரூ.600), so the draft is consistent; however the 'ரூ.15,000 வரை' in slides and '15,000 ரூபாய் மானியம்' in reel_script is stated as a fixed subsidy in the article, not a ceiling ('வரை'), so slides_spec wording 'ரூ.15,000 வரை' introduces an unsupported 'up to' qualifier
  The reel_script states the 1,200 rupee greens kit is sold for 600 rupees, but the article only says the kit is provided 'with a subsidy of ரூ.600', so the selling price is an inference not explicitly stated
  The reel_script and slides omit the article's key fact that the 50% subsidy applies generally and the posting of 'Coimbatore' district scope is only implied by the source headline area, and the reel_script does not mention that the nursery kit listings apply to 'இரண்டு அல்லது மூன்று பழச்செடிகள்' (two or three fruit plants), which is a qualifying detail of the பழச்செடி தொகுப்பு
  The caption's 'Coimbatore home garden subsidy 50 percent' English line is an addition not in the article's content, though it is a translation-style tag rather than a factual claim
